---
description: Reuse demo UI widgets; do not copy the same HTML chrome between demos
globs: **/*.ts,**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: true
---

# Unify demo UI components

Demo HTML that is the same widget must be **one component**, imported.
Do not paste the same JSX into a second `*DemoHelper`.

Demos may cross-import (see `src/README.md`). Upper-layer demos reuse
lower-layer chrome: `formChrome = { ...sectionChrome, renderHeader, renderForm }`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — identical appendix in two helpers
// sectionResponderDemoHelper.tsx
renderAppendix: (comment) => <div style={yellow}>{comment}</div>
// formResponderDemoHelper.tsx
renderAppendix: (comment) => <div style={yellow}>{comment}</div>

// ✅ GOOD — one chrome bag; the form shell adds only form-level slots
export const formChrome = {
  ...sectionChrome,
  renderHeader,
  renderForm,
};
```

Same for `FormContainer`, `PhaseTabs`, lock icons, remark cards, `useFieldMethods`.
Copy-paste is not a variant. If blurbs or fixtures differ, pass them as
**required** props — do not duplicate the widget.

Review follow-up is a nested Design list under the origin item —
`FormDialogsEditor` (`embedded`) plus `followUpEntriesToFlat` /
`syncFollowUpEntriesFromFlat`. Same `AddFormItem`, `FormItemEditor`, Edit, and
move as Design. Do not invent a label-only draft list or a second item editor.

The required star is field-viewer chrome (`RequiredMark`), not draft/list HTML.
If several field viewers show it, they compose the same mark.

Related: `no-html-outside-demo.mdc` (HTML stays in demos),
`no-optional-defaults.mdc` (host/demo still passes copy).
